A grid item's percentage height resolves against its grid area, its containing block, once the rows are sized;
row sizing measures it as auto, since the area's block size is indefinite until then. Percentage min and max
heights still refuse: block formatting would clamp the measured content height against the grid. GridAreaExtent
owns a grid area's extent for columns and rows.

